	(text "Notes\n- Pin names as printed on the ESP32 DevKit V1. On the breadboard only the right-hand row\n  (3V3 ... D23) is reachable; the pins marked with an X are not connected.\n- The DHT22 module has the pull-up resistor for DATA on board.\n- LED resistors are on the cathode side, as built: about 5-6 mA per LED at 3.3 V.\n- The button uses the ESP32's internal pull-up; pressed reads LOW.\n- Power from USB only. Never connect VIN (5 V) to anything else on the board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
